{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits","id":1550687,"title":"Has anyone ever used wraiths and spectres as Werewolf's spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-05-05T08:24:37-07:00","id":1550687,"title":"Has anyone ever used wraiths and spectres as Werewolf's spirits?","content":"Hello, everyone.<br /> <br /> As the title says, I'd love to use ghosts in my W5 games but, really, I don't have neither Wraith core book nor the time to read and learn another system of supernatural powers (arcanos, in this case).<br /> <br /> So, has anyone used ghosts (wraiths and specters) in a Werewolf chronicle, but using Umbral spirits' stats and charms, as described in both W5 and M5?<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to convert them both to umbral spirits as described in WW? If yes, have other STs in here ever stat'ted different specter types?<br /> <br /> Sorry if this sounds silly, I only have a very superficial knowledge of Wraith, but given the little I know about WtO, using them would enrich my Werewolf chronicle.<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28735,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","user":"Greywolf76","date":". 05-05-2025, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T13:35:59-07:00","id":1550705,"title":"","content":"Hey, folks. It's me again. I've found some free time today and tried to make something up, starting with Striplings. Tell me what you think:<br /> <br /> <b>STRIPLINGS</b><br /> A Stripling appears as a gaunt, childlike ghost, its plasmic form flickering with eerie, hollow eyes and a mocking smile. Driven by Oblivion\u2019s urge to grow their ranks, these Spectres haunt the Umbra\u2019s darkest corners, whispering to lonely living children and luring them into deadly traps. Alone, they are weak, but their numbers and cunning make them a sinister threat.<br /> <br /> <b>Rage </b>5, <b>Gnosis </b>4, <b>Willpower </b>5 <b>Essence </b>14<br /> <b>Charms:</b> All Common Charms, plus Beckoning*, Corruption, False Friend*, Whispered Dare*<br /> <br /> <i>Beckoning</i>: The Stripling conjures a faint, alluring glow, sound or ghostly object (e.g., a shimmering light, a giggling voice, children singing nursery rhymes, or a red balloon floating towards danger) that draws children toward a dangerous location (e.g., a cliff edge, a busy road, or a deep well). The lure preys on children\u2019s curiosity, making it hard to resist following. Roll Gnosis (4) vs. the child\u2019s Willpower (difficulty 6). Success compels the child to move toward the designated location for one scene, ignoring obvious dangers unless physically stopped or succeeding on a Willpower roll (difficulty 8). It is usable across the Gauntlet and costs 2 Essence.<br /> <br /> <i>False Friend</i>: The Stripling manifests as a spectral child, visible only to its target, appearing as a friendly playmate who encourages dangerous group activities (e.g., \u201cLet\u2019s all jump off the bridge!\u201d). This illusion fosters trust, making the child more susceptible to the Stripling\u2019s influence. Roll Gnosis (4) vs. the target child\u2019s Wits + Awareness (difficulty 6, typically 3\u20135 dice for a child). Success creates the illusion for one scene, granting a -2 difficulty to subsequent Charms like Whispered Dare or Corruption when targeting that child. Only one child can be targeted at a time, and adults may notice odd behavior (Wits + Awareness, difficulty 8, to sense something supernatural). Requires the Stripling to be in the Umbra or materialized. This Charm costs 2 Essence per use.<br /> <br /> <i>Whispered Dare</i>: The Stripling plants a compelling suggestion in a child\u2019s mind, urging them to take a reckless or dangerous action (e.g., climbing a dangerous tree, exploring a condemned building, or provoking a wild animal). The suggestion appears as a playful dare or an enticing whisper, often disguised as coming from a friend or imaginary playmate. Roll the Stripling\u2019s Gnosis (4) vs. the child\u2019s Willpower (typically 2-4 for children). Success implants the suggestion, compelling the child to act on it within the scene unless interrupted (e.g., by a parent or a successful Willpower roll, difficulty 7). This Charm costs 1 Essence per use.<br /> <br /> <b>Storyteller\u2019s Notes:</b> This version of Striplings drawn a lot from tales of ghost children that target small children and exploit their vulnerabilities. Their new Charms described above evoke the eerie, manipulative nature of ghostly children, drawing on folklore tropes like luring victims to dangerous places (e.g., cliffs, rivers, or abandoned buildings) or encouraging reckless behavior.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-05T17:47:26-07:00","id":1550710,"title":"","content":"I think it is perfectly fine to restat ghosts to the spirit mechanics of WtA if that makes it easier for you to run. You may just need to create your own Charms to best emulate typical ghost hauntings. I'd also make sure that any such ghosts are actually in the Dark Umbra, and not found in the Penumbra. The netherworld of the dead and the spirit world should be separate places.<br /> <br /> In terms of the appropriateness of a ghost's Rage, Gnosis, Willpower, and Essence, just be ready to make adjustments to the needs of the story. If you find your ghost to be too powerful or weak, change things so you hit that sweet spot.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are a staple of gothic literature, horror stories, and spooky stories in general. I don't think they're out of place in any of the other WoD games. Things can get complicated if PCs want to take things to the Underworld itself, but self contained hauntings in the Realm are great and can be easily managed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T05:27:05-07:00","id":1550734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550710#post1550710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is perfectly fine to restat ghosts to the spirit mechanics of WtA if that makes it easier for you to run. You may just need to create your own Charms to best emulate typical ghost hauntings.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I was trying to do with the Stripling (see my second post above). Instead of trying to make an exact stat-by-stat conversion I thought it would be easier to create new charms based on the fluff about that particular type of specter. Although, to be honest, my version leans more on folklore and urban legends of &quot;ghostly children&quot; than WtO's Striplings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550710#post1550710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd also make sure that any such ghosts are actually in the Dark Umbra, and not found in the Penumbra. The netherworld of the dead and the spirit world should be separate places.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550710#post1550710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts are a staple of gothic literature, horror stories, and spooky stories in general. I don't think they're out of place in any of the other WoD games. Things can get complicated if PCs want to take things to the Underworld itself, but self contained hauntings in the Realm are great and can be easily managed..</div> </div> </div> </div>You have excellent points.<br /> <br /> I like having the Dark Umbra (or Underworld) as a distinct part of the Umbra that is inhabited by angry ghosts and spectres with some direct connection to the physical world (easily crossed by ghosts, and quite hard for Garou, who'd probably need some rare mystical rite to get there). It could be a dark place filled with ectoplasmic mists, a gloomy, dark, and dreary land - not unlike Greek Hades.<br /> <br /> But I definitely do not want to use Wraith's lore because it's more than what I really need.<br /> <br /> Also, while trying to adapt the Stipling above, it came to me that instead of trying to adapt Wraith's specters it would be better to just have ghosts that are heavily inspired by traditional and contemporary ghost folklore and urban legends, Gothic novels, and spooky stories that are told around the fire. These ghosts could be occasional antagonists or minions of some sorcerer that dabbles in &quot;necromancy&quot; (the path of <i>summoning, binding &amp; warding</i> as applied to ghosts)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550710#post1550710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the appropriateness of a ghost's Rage, Gnosis, Willpower, and Essence, just be ready to make adjustments to the needs of the story. If you find your ghost to be too powerful or weak, change things so you hit that sweet spot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Applying umbral spirits' stats to traditional ghost types would be the best and easiest option.<br /> <br /> Also, there are plenty of Charms from Werewolf and Mage that would fit traditional ghosts: appear, agony, short out, inhabit, domination, inner pain, and soul reading, for example. I might create another Charm that allows ghosts to perform tasks that require fine motor coordination (writing something with a pen, typing in a typewriter, or pushing the plaquette on an ouija board).<br /> <br /> Also, both <i>Hunter Storyteller Companion</i> and <i>The Walking Dead</i> have stats for materialized ghosts and a huge list of powers (called &quot;spirit tricks&quot;) that could easily be used as ghost charms pretty much as they are.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for your answer and suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T05:46:25-07:00","id":1550735,"title":"","content":"Some examples can be found around the books, most notably in material about the Beast Courts, since they deal with ghosts way more often; this also extends to KotE material, since it used the same spirit system as W:tA and has a number of ghosts simplified into that form.<br /> <br /> And if you want an example of the world's most terrifying Stripling, there's the Innocents from the Mokole Breedbook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T07:33:26-07:00","id":1550737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550735#post1550735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some examples can be found around the books, most notably in material about the Beast Courts, since they deal with ghosts way more often; this also extends to KotE material, since it used the same spirit system as W:tA and has a number of ghosts simplified into that form.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know about Hengeyokai but I didn't know about ghosts and spirits in KotE. Thanks for pointing that out, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> ! Do you know which KotE books (besides the core book) have ghost / spirits in them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550735#post1550735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if you want an example of the world's most terrifying Stripling, there's the Innocents from the Mokole Breedbook.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been ages since I've read the Mokol\u00e9 Breedbook. Thanks for reminding me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T16:07:47-07:00","id":1550771,"title":"","content":"I remeber a reading about a wraith adjacent spirt on this forum called the silver hatred a while back. The post about it heavily implied it used to to be a young hunter who lived during the Impergium and witnessed his village getting wiped out by the garou.<br /> <br /> Which lead to him on the parth to becoming a spirt of vengeance against the garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-06T19:33:47-07:00","id":1550777,"title":"","content":"Honestly, aside from the KotE core, there don't seem to be too many more details like that. From the Devil-Tigers Dharma Book, there's the rite, Deceptive Jade Chains of Yin Demon Command, which allows them to bind beings that have fallen to their Shadows, or plasmics, into their service, much as they bind banes and other unclean Middle Umbral denizens. The book notes that if you have the books and the alternate stats, you can substitute Charisma + Being for a generic spirit Willpower stat.<br /> <br /> For spirits, there's the Unwholesome Nightmare-Inducing Ghost and Unrighteous Cult-Wielding Ghost. Both have Werewolf spirit-style stat blocks, though you're going to have to convert between Power/Chi and Essence, since it's just that old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-09T13:01:39-07:00","id":1550888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550771#post1550771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remeber a reading about a wraith adjacent spirt on this forum called the silver hatred a while back. The post about it heavily implied it used to to be a young hunter who lived during the Impergium and witnessed his village getting wiped out by the garou.<br /> <br /> Which lead to him on the parth to becoming a spirt of vengeance against the garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. This sounds interesting, I'll check it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1550687-has-anyone-ever-used-wraiths-and-spectres-as-werewolf-s-spirits?p=1550777#post1550777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, aside from the KotE core, there don't seem to be too many more details like that. From the Devil-Tigers Dharma Book, there's the rite, Deceptive Jade Chains of Yin Demon Command, which allows them to bind beings that have fallen to their Shadows, or plasmics, into their service, much as they bind banes and other unclean Middle Umbral denizens. The book notes that if you have the books and the alternate stats, you can substitute Charisma + Being for a generic spirit Willpower stat.<br /> <br /> For spirits, there's the Unwholesome Nightmare-Inducing Ghost and Unrighteous Cult-Wielding Ghost. Both have Werewolf spirit-style stat blocks, though you're going to have to convert between Power/Chi and Essence, since it's just that old.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll take a look. Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28735-greywolf76","name":"Greywolf76","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28735_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}